## Project contract changes

### Version control

```markdown
## Version control

Never develop directly on `main`, `master`, `develop`, or `default`. Create each
task branch from an up-to-date `develop` using `feature/<short-slug>` and use it for
the whole task.

Run the relevant checks before committing. Commit every coherent, independently
verifiable increment instead of accumulating the whole task in one commit. Use
`<type>: <what changed and why>` with `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, or
`chore`. Reference an issue or specification when one exists, but neither is
required.

End every agent-authored commit body with a blank line followed by
`Assisted-by: <harness>/<model>/<effort>`.

The final verified result is one full Git object ID. Any subsequent commit
invalidates its review and verification gates.
```

The `<short-slug>` here is the executor-chosen Git branch slug. It is not the topology slug.

### Backlog

`docs/backlog.md` contains only unfinished, deferred, blocked, knowingly unfixed, or unsupported work. Completed entries are deleted. Git is completion history.

### Documentation

Update existing knowledge only when made new or false. Do not create changelogs, migration notes, reports, per-directory READMEs, or cleanup narratives without an explicit requirement or named durable consumer.

Update existing full-turn-retrieval and distribution decisions rather than creating narration documents.

Append original request and clarifications verbatim to `docs/business.md`.

## Error contract

| Condition | Automatic action | Terminal outcome |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Missing Herdr environment or capability | No actor control | Exact `needs_attention` |
| Layout failure | Retry once | `needs_attention` |
| Extra review pane required | Reject construction | Two-pane topology retained |
| Catalogue unavailable | Try supported route | Block only if diversity fails |
| Model absent | Use documented fallback | Block if none launches |
| Selection unprovable | Use supported native default without claiming selection | `selection_unverified` |
| Actor startup failure | One fallback | Recompute diversity |
| Prompt stalls while working | Do not duplicate | Wait |
| Prompt absent while settled | Retry once | Backend blocker |
| Working with progress | Re-arm | Continue |
| Working without progress | Confirm and continue once | External liveness blocker |
| Blocked without handoff | Metadata-only continuation | Backend/external blocker |
| Actor/pane loss | Recreate once, restart gate | Block on repeat |
| Header or boundary damaged | One shorter retry | Unknown/unsupported |
| Row or byte limit exceeded | Request smaller next attempt | Unknown/unsupported on repeat |
| Candidate mismatch or dirty tree | Stop next actor/gate | New clean candidate |
| Reviewer blocker | Finish peer only if candidate intact | Relay after barrier |
| Reviewer QC failure | Finish peer if candidate intact | Executor resolution |
| Finding | Finish peer | Relay all batches |
| Incomplete response batches | Request next/correction | Unknown on repeat |
| First adjudication upholds | Require fix or unresolved dispute | No second same-candidate rebuttal |
| E2E approval needed | Surface class | Resume same session |
| E2E fail | Relay | New candidate |
| E2E unknown | Retry once | Attention |
| New commit | Invalidate all gates | Candidate freeze |
| Secret required in handoff | Do not emit secret | Credentials blocker |
| Hard termination leaves scratch | Never reuse | Best-effort cleanup |

