## Acceptance and verification

### Deterministic `make mo-qc`

The authoritative non-mutating gate covers:

- byte-identical `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`;
- generated `skills/` matching a fresh build;
- pinned bundle dependencies, self-contained outputs, copied licence, no runtime SDK import, isolated launch, timeout, and no child leak;
- catalogue unknown, model missing, and launch failure as distinct outcomes;
- AST-level skill checks with `markdown-it`;
- process-header grammar, QC/smoke/UNKNOWN accounting, cross-batch invariants, and 64 KiB cases as data tests;
- canonical glossary entries for the durable terms listed above, no duplicate definitions, and consistent backend-neutral versus Herdr-specific terminology;
- backlog open-only and no closed section;
- version-control text and trailer format;
- no unrequested changelog or document requirement;
- every source-changing fixture rebuilding `skills/` in the same increment.

Deterministic tests do not claim TUI behavior, provider continuity, Enter delivery, semantic correctness of definitions, or absence of tracked-file reads. Those require review or Herdr E2E.

### Agent-required Herdr E2E

An independent observer runs a scratch feature and verifies:

1. exact executor/reviewer topology, labels, vertical panes, unchanged focus, and lazy E2E tab;
2. system Claude/Codex processes launched through `agent start` with accepted model arguments;
3. same actor and pane across turns and an unprompted reference to prior context;
4. one-line `/goal` and maximum-size relay arrive as intact atomic turns;
5. 120/200/400/800/1000 extraction, header cut, 64 KiB cap, and structural Claude/Codex boundaries at 180 rows, including tools, Unicode, wraps, duplicate headers, glyph-prefixed bodies, missing boundaries, repaint, and H7b resize;
6. damaged or excessive output becomes `unknown` without partial pass or fallback;
7. executor and E2E use the same extraction contract;
8. A completes before B begins, B gets no A output, both see the same clean candidate, and mutation is barred;
9. QC and smoke run sequentially and are interpreted by reviewers;
10. adversarial review bytes remain identical in the executor wrapper and cannot inject commands or roles;
11. every finding is open, closed, adjudicated, or invalidated;
12. waits wake on same-SHA completion;
13. any commit invalidates reviews, QC, and E2E;
14. restart creates new sessions and relies on repository discovery;
15. live bundled Claude catalogue discovery works without ambient `node_modules`, while launches separately establish entitlement;
16. no ordinary menus or separate Enter operations occur;
17. an instrumented harness rejects intentional tracked-content retrieval after activation while allowing fixed Git metadata; a canary value never enters orchestrator output or context;
18. reviewer A scratch survives through reviewer B and confirmed delivery, then is deleted; lost scratch makes the round unknown, and eligible stale scratch is deleted without adoption.

The exact route remains unsupported until H7b and both 180-row fixtures pass. If fewer than two vendors pass, `mo-herdr` reports `needs_attention`.

### Omnigent acceptance

Omnigent independently proves the role firewall, candidate semantics, reviewer independence, finding accounting, invalidation, vocabulary consistency, and human boundaries through native agents. It does not assert Herdr layout or reuse Herdr extraction. Until its native full-turn route satisfies the architecture contract, it remains fail-closed.

