## Rejected and deferred alternatives

Implementation must not regain convenient review retrieval through headless instances, executor-side pane reading, Markdown parsing with `awk`/`sed`, verdict files, semantic finding interpretation, cross-restart state, ordinary human questions, completed backlog history, or routine narration documents.

It must not omit `docs/glossary.md`, define one process term differently across skills, or turn the glossary into a second protocol specification.

It must not claim multi-batch support where a V1 header has no batch identity, accept a syntactically valid but semantically contradictory handoff, repeatedly reset a retry counter within one failing gate, or accept a stale valid header from terminal history.

