The non-mutating gate covers:

- identical `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md`;
- generated tree matching fresh build, including the regenerated `skills/mo-setup/` contract text;
- pinned bundling, measured size ceiling, esbuild-metafile-to-`SHARED_PLAN` licence mapping equality, copied notices, isolation, timeout, and no child leak;
- distinct catalogue/missing/launch outcomes;
- `markdown-it` AST checks;
- full header syntax, blocker phase/source routing, and unknown-class-specific semantic matrices;
- invalid field combinations, identity mismatch, canonical IDs/integers, cumulative accounting, and exact byte limits;
- run-scoped monotonic IDs and invalidation;
- single 180-row/65,536-byte review handoffs and one combined A+B release goal under 135,168 bytes;
- `markdown-it` AST extraction of the literal fenced Node recipe from shipped skill Markdown, followed by execution against `shell:false` argv, random framing delimiter, NUL/UTF-8, trailing-newline, length-mismatch, maximum-size, and failure-output byte fixtures; tests fail if body bytes appear on stdout/stderr;
- state/fingerprint ambiguity outcomes: proven unchanged permits exactly one retry, changed means wait only, contradictory/unproven means attention;
- fail-closed single-handoff V1 for every actor role;
- glossary ownership and qualification;
- complete actor-name collision handling;
- secure current-run scratch and no cross-run discovery;
- open-only backlog, explicit rejection of the existing `## Resolved` history section, and the accepted hard-crash scratch limitation remaining open;
- project-contract version-control text in the root contract and the `mo-setup` source/generated installation instructions;
- exact independent feature-branch regex and installed non-mutating-review-check rule;
- exact pane split/tab-ID commands, replacement-reviewer ID floors, native-goal off/on transitions, and canonical no-progress comparison keys;
- posture probe invocation and structural output classification;
- provider-posture architecture wording matching the self-contained-helper contract;
- no unsolicited documents;
- same-increment generated output.

Golden `recent-unwrapped` captures cover every extraction case that does not require a live alternate-screen repaint and are deterministic fixtures. Deterministic tests do not claim current provider rendering, continuity, Enter delivery, reviewer truth, or absence of tracked reads.

### Agent-required Herdr E2E

